WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan arun da

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.650
<b>Baltigo, Revolutionary 
Army Headquarters</b>

14
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.330
Requesting aid!

15
00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.290
The rebels in Tumi in the South Blue
are becoming outnumbered!

16
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.460
Please come to our aid immediately!

17
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.210
I repeat!

18
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.010
The rebels in Tumi in the South Blue
are becoming outnumbered!

19
00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.680
Please come to our aid immediately!

20
00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.220
We can't go!

21
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.520
We're carrying a lot of injured people
from the Goa Kingdom!

22
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.650
Iva-chan, I'll go.

23
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.610
No, Kuma! You've been too reckless...

24
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.700
...since then!

25
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.200
Kuma!

26
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.870
Wait!

27
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.290
<b>Tumi, South Blue</b>

28
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.590
Damn!

29
00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.710
This is it, rebels!

30
00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:48.810
Is he our ally?

31
00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.110
Ginny got abducted?!

32
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.320
Yes... Seems like a Celestial Dragon
had his eye on her...

33
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.830
She was taken away by a Government ship
to be that Celestial Dragon's wife.

34
00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.610
Ursa Shock.

35
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.790
The Revolutionary Army?

36
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.920
A-Amazing!

37
00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.760
Three years of fighting
has finally paid off!

38
00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.220
All thanks to the Revolutionary Army!

39
00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.770
They're the common people's heroes!

40
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.410
Our unit was wiped out
by an unexpected raid.

41
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.000
I'm sorry!

42
00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.790
I'm so sorry!

43
00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.080
Ring, ring, ring...

44
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:37.920
Clank.

45
00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.590
Dragon, it's me.

46
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.130
I'm tired...

47
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.340
I'll take a ship home.

48
00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:59.020
<b>"A Pledge to Ginny -
Kuma Becomes a Father"</b>

49
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.320
About two years had passed...

50
00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.900
...since Ginny, the 
Revolutionary Army captain,

51
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.610
was kidnapped to be a Celestial
 Dragon's wife...

52
00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.010
I'm sorry.

53
00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.390
We're here, Bonney.

54
00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.450
Kuma! We've got a call from Ginny!

55
00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.530
Move it, babes!

56
00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.870
Ginny!

57
00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.120
Big Bro?

58
00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.330
Ginny!

59
00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.620
Hey, Kumachi!

60
00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.880
I'm back in the lower world!

61
00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.000
Oh! You had us worried!

62
00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.260
Ginny... I'm glad that you're alive!

63
00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:08.970
Yeah...

64
00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.930
I got sick...

65
00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.680
I became unwanted, so I was discarded.

66
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.140
Lucky me!

67
00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.730
Sick?

68
00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.440
What do you mean by that, Ginny?

69
00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.900
I wanted to see you all again,

70
00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.740
but this is me saying goodbye.

71
00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:29.820
Huh?!

72
00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.740
W-What are you talking about, Ginny?!

73
00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.910
I thought I'd never see you again!

74
00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.330
Where are you?! I'll be there right away!

75
00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.670
I'm sorry, Kumachi.

76
00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.170
I'm dying. It won't be long.

77
00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.130
What?

78
00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.220
You're dying?

79
00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.350
Why?

80
00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:58.310
Why?!

81
00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.060
I'll save you!

82
00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.440
I'll leave now!

83
00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.400
Kumachi.

84
00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.200
I appreciate your kindness,
but don't ever come to see me.

85
00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.200
Ginny! We'll be right there to help you!

86
00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.040
Where are you?!

87
00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.040
Move it!

88
00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.170
Kuma!

89
00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:27.920
Where are you going?!

90
00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.630
There's only one place she'd come back to!

91
00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.800
Dragon, Big Bro...

92
00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.770
Kumachi is too kind.
Please watch over him.

93
00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.570
And Kumachi...

94
00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.530
I'll always...

95
00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.200
...always...

96
00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:03.710
...love you.

97
00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.050
Kuma? You're back?!

98
00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.220
Where's Ginny?! I know she's here!

99
00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.020
She is, but...

100
00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.140
Ginny!

101
00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.060
Ginny!

102
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.820
Why... What happened to you?!

103
00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.330
Her face and entire body...

104
00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:45.210
She said when exposed to natural light,
her skin would turn blue and hard like stone.

105
00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.170
Poor child...
I wonder what happened to her.

106
00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.670
Kumachi!

107
00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.180
Yummy!

108
00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.890
Kumachi!

109
00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.980
Let's get married, Kumachi!

110
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.070
I promise I'll make you happy!

111
00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.620
Kumachi!

112
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.210
To make sure her baby could live
even if something happened to her...

113
00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:41.720
...she crossed the sunny seas to get here
while she was still alive.

114
00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.770
Don't worry, Ginny.

115
00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.820
I'll raise your daughter.

116
00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:20.140
No!

117
00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.760
The bottle is at the wrong angle!

118
00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.640
H-H-How's this?

119
00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.520
Oh, sorry!

120
00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.810
Are you trying to drown her?!

121
00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.690
Let me do it!

122
00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.230
Put her in an iron cage when you sleep.

123
00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.820
You might crush her with your massive body.

124
00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.800
She's really cute.

125
00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.630
You drink a lot, Bonney-chan.

126
00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.970
She'll grow up to be a glutton
just like Ginny.

127
00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.180
I want more.

128
00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.730
Yeah, she will...

129
00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.450
Before I knew it, she made it that far away.
I have to keep my eyes on her!

130
00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.580
Yes! That's it, Bonney!

131
00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:37.920
D...

132
00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.340
Daddy!

133
00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.550
Daddy!

134
00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.390
Yes, I'm your daddy!

135
00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.990
Hey! Bonney!

136
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.330
Oh, you're home!

137
00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.410
Welcome home!

138
00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.080
Kuma?!

139
00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:29.840
Why are you boarding up
all the windows in the church?!

140
00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.060
Close the door!

141
00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.270
Look at this.

142
00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.850
Blue stones?!

143
00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.860
This is...

144
00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.320
Just like when Ginny died--

145
00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.280
Don't say it!

146
00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.280
I'll go get the doctor!

147
00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:49.990
Please do...

148
00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:53.990
Well...

149
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.240
When exposed to the sun?

150
00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.750
Really?

151
00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:58.790
Yes.

152
00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.340
Let's take her out and see--

153
00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.840
Don't be ridiculous!

154
00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.970
It's not White Lead Disease...

155
00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:12.590
I'm sorry. I've never seen this symptom.

156
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.850
I see...

157
00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.060
Dad?

158
00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.230
Don't worry, Bonney.

159
00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.610
You're quitting the Revolutionary Army?!

160
00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:27.070
Does Bonney really have
the same disease as her mother?!

161
00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:28.320
Yeah...

162
00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.320
I don't know what to do...

163
00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.490
...but I want to be with her.

164
00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:37.200
I understand.
Live your life without regrets.

165
00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.250
We'll ask every doctor 
in the world that we can.

166
00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.580
Thank you, Dragon!

167
00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.000
<b>Seven</b>

168
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.750
<b>Seven Years Ago</b>

169
00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.050
Time passed, and when Bonney was five...

170
00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.470
Run!

171
00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.720
The vampire will eat us alive!

172
00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.440
<b>Bonney (Age 5)</b>

173
00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.400
Get lost, you little punks!

174
00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.980
Nyaaa!

175
00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.610
Ha! You can't go farther than this point!

176
00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.110
You're a vampire who can't go outside!

177
00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.620
Take this cross! Sheeen!

178
00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.580
Ouch!

179
00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.540
You're in a church!

180
00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.500
You want me to chase you out there?!

181
00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.710
Wait, Bonney!

182
00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.210
Dad.

183
00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:34.180
Please don't go outside. Even just 
seeing you at the door makes me nervous.

184
00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.300
You're such a chicken.
I was just joking.

185
00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.680
Well, don't do it, even as a joke.

186
00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.430
All right.

187
00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.100
I don't wanna make you sad.

188
00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.020
Bonney!

189
00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:50.730
You've grown up to be a good girl!

190
00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.530
Stop it, you crybaby!

191
00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.450
Those punks...

192
00:16:56.320 --> 00:17:00.790
...made fun of the stones on my face!

193
00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:04.160
Is it that weird?

194
00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.420
But it's a disease. I can't help it.

195
00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.540
Those jewels?!

196
00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.540
You scared me!

197
00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:12.130
They're just jealous,
 because they're so beautiful.

198
00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:13.210
What?

199
00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.090
You think so?!

200
00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.510
Yes! I love them!

201
00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:27.020
Bonney, if you were to travel after you
 got well, where would you want to go?

202
00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.730
Oh! Do you know about Sky Islands?

203
00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.190
There are islands in the sky?

204
00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.860
That's right! I saw it in a book!

205
00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.330
See?!

206
00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:46.460
Sky Islands are closer to the sun,
so maybe Nika will be there!

207
00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.250
I bet you'd be excited about that, Daddy!

208
00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.300
Nika, huh?!

209
00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.600
Here we go! Nika's dance!

210
00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.390
It's going to be a big adventure
to go up in the sky!

211
00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.810
Should we do it when you turn 20?

212
00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.520
Okay!

213
00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.270
Where are we going when you turn 19?

214
00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.570
Fish-Man Island!

215
00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:24.790
Your daughter's symptom... It's an 
incurable disease called Sapphire Scales.

216
00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.660
You know what it is?

217
00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:27.580
Yes.

218
00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.500
I'm sorry, but keep your voice down.

219
00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:33.000
I've heard of very few cases recently.

220
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:38.800
Sunlight and moonlight, all kinds of
 natural light will cause the stones to spread.

221
00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:44.600
But even if you avoid the light completely,
it'll still progress.

222
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:45.720
What?

223
00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.270
Is it really incurable?!

224
00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:50.100
Bonney...
My daughter has a way to survive, right?!

225
00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:56.480
I'm going to be honest with you.
Your daughter...

226
00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.280
...has five years at most to live.

227
00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.780
She won't live to see her tenth birthday.

228
00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.950
Can't you do something about it?

229
00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.000
There is no known cure at this time.

230
00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.210
Ten years old?!

231
00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.050
No way...

232
00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.340
But she is growing up to be so healthy!

233
00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.060
Isn't there a cure?

234
00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.110
Are they sure there isn't?!

235
00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.370
What?! Bonney!
I thought you were sleeping!

236
00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.290
I heard that!

237
00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.120
What?

238
00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.370
Ten years old?

239
00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:56.250
Ten years old? What about it?

240
00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.760
I heard someone say ten years old!

241
00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.630
Oh? Are you crying a little bit?

242
00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.840
It was about me, wasn't it?!

243
00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.140
Y-Yeah...

244
00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:08.890
Ten years... Ten years old...

245
00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.520
About your disease, Bonney...

246
00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:15.270
That doctor said you wouldn't get well
until you turn ten years old.

247
00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:16.980
What?

248
00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:21.650
I was just disappointed
that it would take that long.

249
00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.110
Yay!

250
00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.740
I'll get well when I turn ten years old?!

251
00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.490
Can I go on a trip with you?!

252
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:33.370
O-Of course you can!
You'll get better when you turn ten.

253
00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.540
Ya-hoo!

254
00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.380
Oh, no... What have I done?

255
00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:43.260
Then another year passed,

256
00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:47.850
and the nightmare returned to
 the Sorbet Kingdom.

257
00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.560
Kuma!

258
00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.270
Kumachi, help!

259
00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.850
King Bekori did it again!

260
00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.310
It's 16 years ago all over again!

261
00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.440
He's gonna burn alive everyone he thinks 
is weighing the country down!

262
00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:06.200
He's inhuman! 
He's started slaughtering people!

263
00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:32.100
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

264
00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:36.900
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

265
00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.190
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

266
00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.780
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

267
00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.160
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

268
00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:50.660
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

269
00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:56.540
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

270
00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:57.500
We
bokura wa

271
00:21:57.590 --> 00:22:00.000
EVERYDAY owarenai
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end

272
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.630
EVERYDAY makerenai
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated

273
00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:06.390
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

274
00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:08.930
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

275
00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:11.640
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

276
00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:16.940
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

277
00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.690
Don't be afraid
ojikedukuna yo

278
00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:23.650
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

279
00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.110
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

280
00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:28.740
Now, move aside
saa doite

281
00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:31.330
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

282
00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:33.910
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

283
00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:36.620
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

284
00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:39.630
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kiduita no
